@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g6-nouns`
IMPORT `g6-schedule-three`
IMPORT `g6-notice-and-hearing`
IMPORT `g6-amount`

-- g6-warning.l4: ss.52-54.  The administrative warning the Commissioner may give instead of a financial
-- sanction (s.52), the violator's request within 30 days to cancel it (s.53), and what follows when the violator
-- goes on breaching or breaches again after a warning (s.54).
--
-- Clock convention for the regulative rules here: `AT 0` is the day the warning was delivered; an event `AT k`
-- happened k days after it.
--
-- Periods owned here (PLAN section (d)):
--   P33, s.53(a): "within 30 days": a window in which a request may be made, kind W.  The Law gives no anchor;
--     the delivery of the warning is taken (fork F-ANCHOR); IL s.10(a), and IL s.10(c) applied (ruling 4); the
--     alternative without s.10(c) is callable.  The Commissioner may extend it (s.53(b)): kind X, an input date.
--   P34, s.54(b): "within two years of the day the warning was delivered": kind B (a classification window); the
--     calendar arithmetic is IL s.10(b)'s end rule, IL s.10(c) is NOT applied (as for s.45(b), see g6-amount); the
--     reading that applies it is callable.  The day of delivery is outside the window (IL s.10: the day of the
--     event is not counted); the last day is inside.
--
-- Not in the sources: the procedures the Commissioner directs under s.52(a) (their circumstances are an input);
-- whether a cancelled warning still counts under s.54; how long the Commissioner has to decide a request.

§ `Chapter 6: administrative enforcement measures`

§§ `Subchapter B: administrative warning`

§§§ `ss 52 to 54: the acts`

@desc A written decision on a request to cancel a warning (s.53(c)): when delivered, whether in writing and whether it gives reasons
DECLARE `Written decision on a request to cancel a warning` HAS
    `delivered on` IS A DATE @desc The day the decision was delivered to the violator
    `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the decision is in writing
    `states the reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the decision is delivered with its reasons

@desc The acts of ss.52 to 54: giving a warning, the violator's request to cancel it, the Commissioner's extension and decision, the written decision and the notice of intention after a warning; the first field says who performs each act
DECLARE `Act under ss 52 to 54` IS ONE OF
    `give the violator an administrative warning`
        HAS `performed by the warning officer` IS A Party
            `the warning given` IS AN `Administrative warning`
    `ask the Commissioner in writing to cancel the administrative warning`
        HAS `performed by the requesting violator` IS A Party
            `the request is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
            `the ground relied on` IS A `Ground for cancelling a warning`
    `extend the period to ask for cancellation of the warning`
        HAS `performed by the extending officer for a warning` IS A Party
            `the extension granted for a warning` IS AN `Extension granted by the Commissioner`
    `decide a request to cancel an administrative warning`
        HAS `performed by the officer deciding on a request` IS A Party
            `the decision taken on the request` IS A `Decision on a request to cancel a warning`
    `give the violator the decision on the request in writing with reasons`
        HAS `performed by the officer giving the decision` IS A Party
            `the written decision given` IS A `Written decision on a request to cancel a warning`
    `give the violator written notice of intention to impose a financial sanction after a warning`
        HAS `performed by the officer giving notice after a warning` IS A Party
            `the notice given after a warning` IS A `Notice of intention`

§§§ `s 52: the administrative warning`

-- src:395 | {{ח:סעיף|52|התראה מינהלית}}
-- src:396 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} היה לממונה יסוד סביר להניח כי אדם הפר הוראה מההוראות לפי חוק זה, כאמור {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 41|בסעיף 41}}, והתקיימו נסיבות המנויות בנהלים שהורה עליהם הממונה, באישור היועץ המשפטי לממשלה, רשאי הוא במקום להטיל עליו עיצום כספי לפי הוראות {{ח:פנימי|פרק ו סימן א|סימן א׳}}, למסור לו התראה מינהלית לפי הוראות {{ח:פנימי|פרק ו סימן ב|סימן זה}}; בסעיף קטן זה, ”היועץ המשפטי לממשלה“ – לרבות משנה ליועץ המשפטי לממשלה שהיועץ המשפטי לממשלה הסמיכו לעניין זה.
-- (a): the Commissioner may give a warning INSTEAD of a sanction when he has reasonable grounds to think a listed
-- provision was breached and "circumstances listed in procedures that the Commissioner directed, with the approval
-- of the Attorney General" were met.  "Attorney General" includes a deputy the Attorney General authorised.  The
-- grounds, the circumstances and the approval are facts or opinions: inputs.  Chapter 6 in force is G7's.
@ref s.52(a) (src:396)
GIVEN `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner has reasonable grounds to think the person breached a listed provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `circumstances listed in the procedures the Commissioner directed are met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the procedures were approved by the Attorney General or a deputy the Attorney General authorised for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 52(a) — the Commissioner may give an administrative warning instead of a financial sanction` `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` `the Commissioner has reasonable grounds to think the person breached a listed provision` `circumstances listed in the procedures the Commissioner directed are met` `the procedures were approved by the Attorney General or a deputy the Attorney General authorised for the purpose` MEANS
        `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act`
    ... `the Commissioner has reasonable grounds to think the person breached a listed provision`
    ... `circumstances listed in the procedures the Commissioner directed are met`
    AND `the procedures were approved by the Attorney General or a deputy the Attorney General authorised for the purpose`

-- src:397 | {{ח:תת|(ב)}} בהתראה מינהלית יציין הממונה מהו המעשה המהווה את ההפרה ומועד ביצועה, יודיע למפר כי עליו להפסיק את ההפרה וכי אם ימשיך בהפרה או יחזור עליה יהיה צפוי לעיצום כספי בשל הפרה נמשכת או הפרה חוזרת, לפי העניין, כאמור {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 45|בסעיף 45}}, וכן יציין את זכותו של המפר לבקש את ביטול ההתראה לפי הוראות {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 53|סעיף 53}}.
-- (b): the warning states the act and when it was committed, tells the violator to stop, informs him that
-- continuing or repeating exposes him to a sanction for a continuing or repeat violation (s.45), and states his
-- right to ask for cancellation (s.53).
@ref s.52(b) (src:397)
GIVEN warning IS AN `Administrative warning`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 52(b) — the administrative warning states what the Law requires` warning MEANS
        "the act and its date" ... warning's `states the act or omission that is the breach and the date of the breach`
    ... "stop the breach" ... warning's `tells the violator to stop the breach`
    ... "a sanction for a continuing or repeat violation" ... warning's `warns of a sanction for a continuing or repeat violation`
    AND "the right to ask for cancellation" ... warning's `states the violator's right to ask for cancellation under section 53`

@ref s.52(a), s.52(b) (src:396-397)
GIVEN `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner has reasonable grounds to think the person breached a listed provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `circumstances listed in the procedures the Commissioner directed are met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the procedures were approved by the Attorney General or a deputy the Attorney General authorised for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under ss 52 to 54`
`s 52(a) — the Commissioner may give the violator an administrative warning` `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` `the Commissioner has reasonable grounds to think the person breached a listed provision` `circumstances listed in the procedures the Commissioner directed are met` `the procedures were approved by the Attorney General or a deputy the Attorney General authorised for the purpose` MEANS
    IF   `s 52(a) — the Commissioner may give an administrative warning instead of a financial sanction` `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` `the Commissioner has reasonable grounds to think the person breached a listed provision` `circumstances listed in the procedures the Commissioner directed are met` `the procedures were approved by the Attorney General or a deputy the Attorney General authorised for the purpose`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MAY   `give the violator an administrative warning` `the Commissioner` warning
               PROVIDED `s 52(b) — the administrative warning states what the Law requires` warning
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§§ `s 53: a request to cancel the warning, 30 days`

-- src:399 | {{ח:סעיף|53|בקשה לביטול התראה מינהלית}}
-- src:400 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} נמסרה למפר התראה מינהלית כאמור {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 52|בסעיף 52}}, רשאי הוא לפנות לממונה בכתב, בתוך 30 ימים, בבקשה לבטל את ההתראה בשל אחד מהטעמים האלה:
-- src:401 | {{ח:תתת|(1)}} המפר לא ביצע את ההפרה;
-- src:402 | {{ח:תתת|(2)}} המעשה שביצע המפר, המפורט בהתראה, אינו מהווה הפרה.
-- 30 days "within 30 days" with no anchor in the sentence: the delivery of the warning, the event the sentence has
-- just named (fork F-ANCHOR).  Kind W: IL s.10(a), the day of delivery not counted, and IL s.10(c) applied.
@ref s.53(a) (src:400)
GIVEN `the day the 30 days run from` IS A DATE
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 53(a) — the last day of the 30 days from` `the day the 30 days run from` `with` calendar MEANS
    `s 10(a), (c) — the last day of a period of` 30 `days from` `the day the 30 days run from` `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`Chapter 6 — the days of rest, recess or holiday of` calendar)

@ref s.53(a) (src:400)
GIVEN `the day the 30 days run from` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 53(a) — without s 10(c), the last day of the 30 days from` `the day the 30 days run from` MEANS
    `s 10(a) — the last day of a period of` 30 `days from` `the day the 30 days run from`

-- The taken anchor: the delivery of the warning.  The alternative anchor (F-ANCHOR) is the day of the breach
-- that the warning states, the only other day a warning carries.
@ref s.53(a) (src:400)
GIVEN warning IS AN `Administrative warning`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 53(a) — the last day to ask to cancel` warning `counting from its delivery, with` calendar MEANS
    `s 53(a) — the last day of the 30 days from` (warning's `delivered on`) `with` calendar

@ref s.53(a) (src:400)
GIVEN `the day of the breach` IS A DATE
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 53(a) — the last day to ask to cancel, counting from the day of the breach` `the day of the breach` `with` calendar MEANS
    `s 53(a) — the last day of the 30 days from` `the day of the breach` `with` calendar

-- (b): the Commissioner may extend the period, for special reasons that shall be recorded.  An extension
-- without recorded reasons is ignored (as at s.43, fork F-EXT).
-- src:403 | {{ח:תת|(ב)}} הממונה רשאי להאריך את התקופה האמורה בסעיף קטן (א), מטעמים מיוחדים שיירשמו.
@ref s.53(b) (src:403)
@export The last day on which a violator may ask in writing for an administrative warning to be cancelled: 30 days from its delivery, moved past days of rest, recess or holiday, or the day an extension granted for recorded special reasons ends when that is later
GIVEN warning IS AN `Administrative warning` @desc The administrative warning: to whom it was given, which item it concerns, when it was delivered, what it states and whether it was cancelled
      extension IS A MAYBE `Extension granted by the Commissioner` @desc The extension the Commissioner granted, if any: the day the period now ends and whether special reasons were recorded; NOTHING if none was granted
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days` @desc The days of rest, recess or holiday under an enactment for the years the question touches, as a list of dates (never computed)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 53(a), (b) — the last day to ask to cancel` warning `counting from its delivery, given` extension `with` calendar MEANS
    CONSIDER extension
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 53(a) — the last day to ask to cancel` warning `counting from its delivery, with` calendar
    WHEN JUST granted THEN
        IF   granted's `special reasons were recorded`
        THEN `Chapter 6 — the later of` (granted's `the period now ends on`) `and` (`s 53(a) — the last day to ask to cancel` warning `counting from its delivery, with` calendar)
        ELSE `s 53(a) — the last day to ask to cancel` warning `counting from its delivery, with` calendar

-- Fork F-SHORTEN (as at s.43): the extension is the period's end whatever day the Commissioner chose, even one before
-- the 30 days are out.  The reading taken is that "extend" cannot shorten, so the 30 days stand.
@ref s.53(b) (src:403)
GIVEN warning IS AN `Administrative warning`
      extension IS A MAYBE `Extension granted by the Commissioner`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 53(b) — taking an extension that ends before the 30 days as it is, the last day to ask to cancel` warning `counting from its delivery, given` extension `with` calendar MEANS
    CONSIDER extension
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 53(a) — the last day to ask to cancel` warning `counting from its delivery, with` calendar
    WHEN JUST granted THEN
        IF   granted's `special reasons were recorded`
        THEN granted's `the period now ends on`
        ELSE `s 53(a) — the last day to ask to cancel` warning `counting from its delivery, with` calendar

-- Is a day timely, within the s.53 period?  A request made on the day the warning is delivered is "within 30 days" of it
-- (fork F-ACTDAY, as at s.43): the day of delivery or later, and the last day or earlier; the last day is inside.
@ref s.53(a) (src:400)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      warning IS AN `Administrative warning`
      extension IS A MAYBE `Extension granted by the Commissioner`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 53(a) — the day` day `is within the period to ask to cancel` warning `given` extension `with` calendar MEANS
        (warning's `delivered on` AT MOST day)
    AND (day AT MOST `s 53(a), (b) — the last day to ask to cancel` warning `counting from its delivery, given` extension `with` calendar)

-- Fork F-ACTDAY: the strict reading, the period beginning the day AFTER delivery.
@ref s.53(a) (src:400)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      warning IS AN `Administrative warning`
      extension IS A MAYBE `Extension granted by the Commissioner`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 53(a) — counting the day after delivery as the first day, the day` day `is within the period to ask to cancel` warning `given` extension `with` calendar MEANS
    `s 8, s 10 — the date` day `is inside the period beginning on` (`s 10 — the first day of a period counted from or after an event on` (warning's `delivered on`)) `and ending on` (`s 53(a), (b) — the last day to ask to cancel` warning `counting from its delivery, given` extension `with` calendar)

@ref s.53(a) (src:400)
GIVEN warning IS AN `Administrative warning`
      extension IS A MAYBE `Extension granted by the Commissioner`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 53(a), (b) — the days from the delivery of` warning `to the last day to ask to cancel, given` extension `with` calendar MEANS
    (Day (`s 53(a), (b) — the last day to ask to cancel` warning `counting from its delivery, given` extension `with` calendar)) MINUS (Day (warning's `delivered on`))

-- The right: the violator MAY ask in writing, on one of the two grounds, within the period.  The two grounds are
-- the cases of `Ground for cancelling a warning`, so a request on any other ground cannot be written.
@ref s.53(a) (src:400-402)
GIVEN warning IS AN `Administrative warning`
      extension IS A MAYBE `Extension granted by the Commissioner`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under ss 52 to 54`
`s 53(a) — the violator may ask for the warning to be cancelled` warning extension calendar MEANS
    IF   NOT warning's `cancelled under section 53`
    THEN PARTY  `the violator`
         MAY    `ask the Commissioner in writing to cancel the administrative warning` `the violator` inWriting ground
                PROVIDED inWriting
         WITHIN (`s 53(a), (b) — the days from the delivery of` warning `to the last day to ask to cancel, given` extension `with` calendar)
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref s.53(b) (src:403)
GIVEN `the Commissioner finds special reasons for an extension` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under ss 52 to 54`
`s 53(b) — the Commissioner may extend the period to ask for cancellation` `the Commissioner finds special reasons for an extension` MEANS
    IF   `the Commissioner finds special reasons for an extension`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MAY   `extend the period to ask for cancellation of the warning` `the Commissioner` granted
               PROVIDED granted's `special reasons were recorded`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (c): on a request the Commissioner may cancel the warning, or refuse and leave it in place; the decision is
-- given in writing and delivered with reasons.  The choice is his: an input (the decision).
-- src:404 | {{ח:תת|(ג)}} קיבל הממונה בקשה לביטול התראה מינהלית, לפי הוראות סעיף קטן (א), רשאי הוא לבטל את ההתראה או לדחות את הבקשה ולהותיר את ההתראה על כנה; החלטת הממונה תינתן בכתב ותימסר למפר בצירוף נימוקים.
@ref s.53(c) (src:404)
GIVEN `a request was made within the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      decision IS A `Decision on a request to cancel a warning`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under ss 52 to 54`
`s 53(c) — the Commissioner decides a request to cancel the warning` `a request was made within the period` decision MEANS
    IF   `a request was made within the period`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MAY   `decide a request to cancel an administrative warning` `the Commissioner` decision
         HENCE ( PARTY `the Commissioner`
                 MUST  `give the violator the decision on the request in writing with reasons` `the Commissioner` written
                       PROVIDED `s 53(c) — the decision is in writing and gives reasons` written )
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref s.53(c) (src:404)
GIVEN written IS A `Written decision on a request to cancel a warning`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 53(c) — the decision is in writing and gives reasons` written MEANS
        "in writing" ... written's `in writing`
    AND "with reasons" ... written's `states the reasons`

§§§ `s 54: a continuing or repeat violation after a warning`

-- src:406 | {{ח:סעיף|54|הפרה נמשכת והפרה חוזרת לאחר התראה}}
-- src:407 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} נמסרה למפר התראה מינהלית לפי הוראות {{ח:פנימי|פרק ו סימן ב|סימן זה}} והמפר המשיך להפר את ההוראה שבשלה נמסרה לו ההתראה, יראו את ההפרה כאמור כהפרה נמשכת לעניין {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 45|סעיף 45(א)}}, והממונה ימסור למפר הודעה על כוונת חיוב בשל ההפרה הנמשכת, בהתאם להוראות {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 42|סעיף 42}}, בשינויים המחויבים.
-- src:408 | {{ח:תת|(ב)}} נמסרה למפר התראה מינהלית לפי הוראות {{ח:פנימי|פרק ו סימן ב|סימן זה}} והמפר חזר והפר את ההוראה שבשלה נמסרה לו ההתראה, בתוך שנתיים מיום מסירת ההתראה, יראו את ההפרה הנוספת כאמור כהפרה חוזרת לעניין {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 45|סעיף 45(ב)}}, והממונה ימסור למפר הודעה על כוונת חיוב בשל ההפרה החוזרת, בהתאם להוראות {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 42|סעיף 42}}, בשינויים המחויבים.
-- A warning the Commissioner cancelled under s.53 is no warning: s.54 speaks of a violator "to whom an
-- administrative warning was delivered" and a cancelled one was delivered and then undone; the reading taken is
-- that cancellation undoes it (fork F-CANCEL), and the alternative that ignores the cancellation is callable.
-- The provision the warning "concerned" follows from the Third Schedule item the warning names.
@ref s.54(a) (src:407)
GIVEN warning IS AN `Administrative warning`
      `the listed violation of the further breach` IS A `Listed violation`
      `the violator continued to breach after the warning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 54(a) — a breach continued after` warning `is treated as a continuing violation, the further breach being` `the listed violation of the further breach` `and the violator having continued:` `the violator continued to breach after the warning` MEANS
        "the warning was not cancelled" ... NOT warning's `cancelled under section 53`
    ... "the same provision" ... `Third Schedule — the provision contravened by` (warning's `the listed violation the warning concerns`) EQUALS `Third Schedule — the provision contravened by` `the listed violation of the further breach`
    AND "the violator continued to breach it" ... `the violator continued to breach after the warning`

@ref s.54(a) (src:407)
GIVEN warning IS AN `Administrative warning`
      `the listed violation of the further breach` IS A `Listed violation`
      `the violator continued to breach after the warning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 54(a) — ignoring any cancellation, a breach continued after` warning `is treated as a continuing violation, the further breach being` `the listed violation of the further breach` `and the violator having continued:` `the violator continued to breach after the warning` MEANS
        "the same provision" ... `Third Schedule — the provision contravened by` (warning's `the listed violation the warning concerns`) EQUALS `Third Schedule — the provision contravened by` `the listed violation of the further breach`
    AND "the violator continued to breach it" ... `the violator continued to breach after the warning`

-- The months of the continuing violation (P28): from the day the breach began, or (F-START) from the delivery of the
-- warning.  Both are counts of whole months, IL s.10(b); the Law says only that s.45(a) applies.
@ref s.54(a) (src:407)
GIVEN `the day the breach began` IS A DATE
      `the last day the breach continued` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 54(a) — the months of a continuing violation counted from the day the breach began` `the day the breach began` `until` `the last day the breach continued` MEANS
    `s 45(a) — the whole months a violation continued from` `the day the breach began` `to` `the last day the breach continued`

@ref s.54(a) (src:407)
GIVEN warning IS AN `Administrative warning`
      `the last day the breach continued` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 54(a) — the months of a continuing violation counted from the delivery of` warning `until` `the last day the breach continued` MEANS
    `s 45(a) — the whole months a violation continued from` (warning's `delivered on`) `to` `the last day the breach continued`

-- (b): within two years of the day the warning was delivered.  P34, kind B.  The day of delivery is outside the
-- window, the last day is inside.
@ref s.54(b) (src:408)
GIVEN warning IS AN `Administrative warning`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 54(b) — the last day of the two years from the delivery of` warning MEANS
    `s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 2 `years after an event on` (warning's `delivered on`)

@ref s.54(b) (src:408)
GIVEN warning IS AN `Administrative warning`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 54(b) — the last day of the two years from the delivery of` warning `, when s 10(c) applies, with` calendar MEANS
    `s 10(b), (c) — the last day of a period of` 2 `years after an event on` (warning's `delivered on`) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`Chapter 6 — the days of rest, recess or holiday of` calendar)

@ref s.54(b) (src:408)
GIVEN warning IS AN `Administrative warning`
      violation IS A Violation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 54(b) — the further violation after` warning `is treated as a repeat violation:` violation MEANS
        "the warning was not cancelled" ... NOT warning's `cancelled under section 53`
    ... "the same violator" ... warning's `the violator`'s `reference for the person` EQUALS violation's `the violator`'s `reference for the person`
    ... "the same provision" ... `Third Schedule — the provision contravened by` (warning's `the listed violation the warning concerns`) EQUALS `Third Schedule — the provision contravened by` (violation's `the listed violation`)
    ... "after the delivery" ... warning's `delivered on` LESS THAN violation's `date of the act`
    AND "within two years" ... violation's `date of the act` AT MOST `s 54(b) — the last day of the two years from the delivery of` warning

@ref s.54(b) (src:408)
GIVEN warning IS AN `Administrative warning`
      violation IS A Violation
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 54(b) — with s 10(c) applied to the window, the further violation after` warning `is treated as a repeat violation:` violation `, with` calendar MEANS
        "the warning was not cancelled" ... NOT warning's `cancelled under section 53`
    ... "the same violator" ... warning's `the violator`'s `reference for the person` EQUALS violation's `the violator`'s `reference for the person`
    ... "the same provision" ... `Third Schedule — the provision contravened by` (warning's `the listed violation the warning concerns`) EQUALS `Third Schedule — the provision contravened by` (violation's `the listed violation`)
    ... "after the delivery" ... warning's `delivered on` LESS THAN violation's `date of the act`
    AND "within two years" ... violation's `date of the act` AT MOST `s 54(b) — the last day of the two years from the delivery of` warning `, when s 10(c) applies, with` calendar

-- The Commissioner "shall" deliver a notice of intention under s.42, with the necessary changes, for the continuing
-- or repeat violation.  s.42(a) makes the duty depend on his intention to impose; s.54 does not repeat the
-- condition and says "shall" (fork F-MUST54): the reading taken is a duty whenever s.54(a) or (b) applies; the
-- alternative that keeps s.42(a)'s condition is callable.  No time limit is stated, so no WITHIN.
@ref s.54(a), s.54(b) (src:407-408)
GIVEN `s 54(a) or (b) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under ss 52 to 54`
`s 54 — the Commissioner must give notice of intention after a warning` `s 54(a) or (b) applies` MEANS
    IF   `s 54(a) or (b) applies`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MUST  `give the violator written notice of intention to impose a financial sanction after a warning` `the Commissioner` notice
               PROVIDED `s 42(b) — the notice of intention states what the Law requires` notice
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref s.54(a), s.54(b), s.42(a) (src:407-408)
GIVEN `s 54(a) or (b) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner intends to impose a financial sanction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under ss 52 to 54`
`s 54 — the Commissioner must give notice of intention after a warning, if he intends to impose a sanction` `s 54(a) or (b) applies` `the Commissioner intends to impose a financial sanction` MEANS
    IF   `s 54(a) or (b) applies` AND `the Commissioner intends to impose a financial sanction`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MUST  `give the violator written notice of intention to impose a financial sanction after a warning` `the Commissioner` notice
               PROVIDED `s 42(b) — the notice of intention states what the Law requires` notice
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED
